# Leaks this project has judged and forgiven, so that a run reporting
# nothing else means something (project.md sec 16.100).
#
# A suppression is a claim, so each one names what it forgives and why.
# Anything not listed here still fails the run, which is the point: a
# sanitized suite that is always red is one nobody reads, and this one
# was always red for a single Qt-internal allocation.

# QScroller::grabGesture registers a gesture recogniser that Qt keeps for
# the life of the process. 256 bytes in 16 allocations, one per window
# the suite builds. Judged in sec 16.83 as not ours, and re-tested in sec
# 16.100: ungrabbing on destruction does not release it and adds two
# allocations of its own, which is Qt saying the recogniser is not the
# caller's to free.
leak:QScroller::grabGesture
